  "verbalization": "Perphenazine, a member of the phenothiazine class, is linked to Calm2 through a series of molecular and pharmacological relationships. The evidence suggests that Perphenazine, as part of the phenothiazine family, binds to Calm2, with the lowest common ancestor between Perphenazine and Trifluoperazine being the phenothiazine class. This implies a shared pharmacological profile, where the structural similarity between Perphenazine and Trifluoperazine, along with their binding to Calm2, supports a functional relationship. Additionally, the resemblance between Perphenazine and Clocapramine, which also binds to Calm2, further reinforces the notion that Perphenazine may share a similar mechanism of action with other compounds in the same class. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Perphenazine exerts its effects on Calm2, likely through a common pharmacological pathway involving the phenothiazine class and its interaction with the target protein.",
